  "question": {
    "text": "For an integer $\\mathrm{n} \\geq 2$, if the arithmetic mean of all coefficients in the binomial expansion of $(x+y)^{2 n-3}$ is 16 , then the distance of the point $P\\left(2 n-1, n^2-4 n\\right)$ from the line $x+y=8$ is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "NGT4C",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "eaLLK",
      "text": "$2 \\sqrt{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "aKOEo",
      "text": "$5 \\sqrt{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "c9o3t",
      "text": "$3 \\sqrt{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "No. of terms in $(x+y)^{(2 n-3)} \\Rightarrow\\left[\\begin{array}{c}(2 n-3+1) \\\\ (2 n-2)\\end{array}\\right].$ \n$\\therefore$ sum of all coefficients $=2^{2 n-3}$\n(Put $\\mathrm{x}=\\mathrm{y}=1$ )\n$\\therefore$ Arithmetic mean of all coefficients\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& =\\left(\\frac{2^{2 n-3}}{2 n-2}\\right)=16 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow 2^{2 n-3}=2^5(n-1) \\Rightarrow n=5 \\\\\n& \\therefore P\\left(2 n-1, n^2-4 n\\right)=(9,5)\n\\end{aligned}$\n\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/zQOPegNaGroihIXObDobjfcSVyZC8NsiEeh7ci6YInA.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>\n\n$\\begin{aligned} & x+y=8 \\\\ & \\therefore P M=\\left|\\frac{9+5-8}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right|=\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{3 \\times 2}{\\sqrt{2}}=3 \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
